<title>GREECE: XIOSBANK CUTS MORTGAGE RATE BY 100BPS TO 15PCT.</title>
<headline>XIOSBANK CUTS MORTGAGE RATE BY 100BPS TO 15PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private Xiosbank cut its mortgage rate by 100 basis points to 15 percent following January's lower CPI inflation figure which eased to 6.8 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Xiosbank said it had lent over 18.5 billion drachmas in housing loans to over 5,000 clients.</p>
<p>It is also dropping its savings deposit rate by a quarter of a point to 10.0 percent.</p>
<p>All base loan rates remain unchanged, it said. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
